WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:05.090
- You've made so many great
shows and movies in your career.

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:09.750
So many that we've enjoyed so much.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.640
And I watched your-
- Well, likewise.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:12.473
- Oh, thank you.

00:00:12.473 --> 00:00:15.290
Well, I watched your
new show, "Severance."

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:17.113
- Oh, cool.
- I mean-

00:00:17.113 --> 00:00:20.600
(audience applauding)

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.840
- What'd you think?
- It's so...

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:25.636
First of all, it's
directed by Ben Stiller.

00:00:25.636 --> 00:00:27.780
I'm loving watching it.

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.550
Tell us about it.
- Oh, thank you.

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.050
I'm so glad you like it.

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:34.990
Yeah, and you know Ben, you
know what a brilliant guy he is

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:38.170
and he had this vision,

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:40.700
and Dan Erickson, who
created the show as well,

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.100
but Ben kind of took it and came up

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:46.160
with a whole visual
language for this world.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:47.730
It really was world building,

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:50.450
cuz there's this whole science fiction,

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.950
and so you have to introduce the audience

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:56.850
to all these circumstances
and this whole world

00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:00.270
of this company and this technology.

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:02.070
The show takes place in a world

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:05.920
where you can have a chip
inserted in your brain,

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.800
so when you go to work,

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.620
you take an elevator down to the office

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:12.790
and on that elevator ride,
the chip is triggered,

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:13.810
so when you're down there,

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:16.600
you have no idea who you
are in the outside world,

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.070
you have no access to those memories.

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:22.170
Your entire life and
world is there at work.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.560
And then when you leave
work at the end of the day,

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:27.400
it's triggered again and
you're in the outside world,

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:30.420
but have no memory of what
you did at work that day.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:31.253
So you have these

00:01:31.253 --> 00:01:33.270
two separate lives.
- How wild is that?

00:01:34.213 --> 00:01:35.303
(audience applauding)
I mean.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:40.490
- Yeah, it's really
cool. It's a cool idea.

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:41.323
It's really fun.

00:01:41.323 --> 00:01:42.660
- I was... I really...

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:46.900
I knew that going in and
it didn't ruin it for me.

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:49.727
It helped it and I loved it and I think,

00:01:49.727 --> 00:01:54.727
"What an incredible premise
for life, a show, a debate?"

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:58.228
It's so rich, really.

00:01:58.228 --> 00:02:00.895
(upbeat music)

